-- Schema version 4 to 5 (Phase 2, PR 6b, ADR 0068).
--
-- A terminal occurrence is immutable in full. The trigger from version 2 aborted a change of state out of a
-- terminal state and nothing else, so an update of a terminal row's instant, zone, date or slot was allowed by the
-- schema. The time zone change is the first path that changes an instant, and ARCHITECTURE.md 3.2 says terminal
-- occurrences are immutable, so the schema now says exactly that: any update to a row whose OLD state is COMPLETED,
-- SKIPPED or MISSED aborts. There is no sanctioned update to a terminal row.
--
-- A trigger cannot be altered, so it is dropped and created again under the same name. DROP TRIGGER and CREATE
-- TRIGGER work on the SQLite 3.22 floor (ADR 0042). No data changes.

DROP TRIGGER occurrence_terminal_immutable;

CREATE TRIGGER occurrence_terminal_immutable
BEFORE UPDATE ON occurrence
WHEN old.state IN ('COMPLETED', 'SKIPPED', 'MISSED')
BEGIN
    SELECT RAISE(ABORT, 'terminal occurrence is immutable');
END;
